bythepond-by-tkln (1.0-0ddebs4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changes prepared with Claude Opus 5.5
  * debian/control : depend on libsdl1.2debian only: on Debian 12,
    libsdl1.2-compat installs libSDL-1.2.so.0 outside of the library
    path and the intro could not dlopen it
  * debian/control : added libgl1 (opened with dlopen), removed the
    hardcoded libc6, wrote a real description
  * debian/copyright : no license found upstream, use public-domain
    (probably freeware) instead of GPL-3.0+, Source is the scene.org
    release
  * debian/resources : added the missing icon (the PNG was empty),
    cropped from the Pouet screenshot
  * debian/README.source : explain the content of the orig tarball and
    the dlopen dependencies
  * debian/bythepond-by-tkln.6.md : documented --help and the sdl12-
    compat slowdown
  * debian/docs : removed the empty file
  * debian/bythepond-by-tkln.lintian-overrides : override the pandoc
    groff-message
  * debian/rules, debian/shlibs-stub.c : compute the shlibs on a stub
    with the same imports, dpkg-shlibdeps cannot read the packed
    executable (no section header table)

 -- Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:25:49 +0100

